From: Connor Clark
Subject: [PATCH] fix(zc): use the quest given on the command line for standalone saves

In standalone mode, an existing save file kept using the quest path it
recorded when it was created, ignoring the quest given on the command
line. Under Flatpak, a quest opened from outside the sandbox's folders
gets a document portal path, so its save stayed tied to that path even
after access to the quest's real folder was granted, and enhanced music
next to the quest never loaded.

Backport for 2.55.18; remove when updating to a release with the fix.
---
--- a/src/zc/zelda.cpp
+++ b/src/zc/zelda.cpp
@@ -1418,6 +1418,12 @@
 	chop_path(qstpath);
 	int32_t ret = 0;
 	int32_t qst_num = g->get_quest();
+
+	// In standalone mode, play the quest given on the command line, even if the save
+	// file recorded a different path for it (the quest was moved, or a sandbox like
+	// Flatpak handed it over from a different location last time).
+	if (standalone_mode && !standalone_quest.empty())
+		g->header.qstpath = standalone_quest.string();
 
 	if (g->header.qstpath.empty() && !qst_num)
 	{
